# YUMI: bowden backlash take-up -- dense layer change, the "Invalid sequence"
# crash. BACKLASH_DEDUCT + BACKLASH_BLEED active, reversals closer than the
# 58.9 ms ramp: without the no-overlap insertion invariant, the commanded
# offset jumps and stepcompress refuses the sequence.
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG backlash_layer_change.cfg

G28
G1 X20 Y20 Z1 F6000
M83
# Exact parameters of the real crash: long ramp (58.9 ms), deduct + bleed
SET_PRESSURE_ADVANCE ADVANCE=0 SMOOTH_TIME=0 LEAD_TIME=0 BOWDEN_LENGTH=800 BACKLASH_COEF=1 BACKLASH_SPEED=40 BACKLASH_ACCEL=15000 BACKLASH_DEDUCT=0.5 BACKLASH_BLEED=10
# Settle into forward extrusion first
G1 X30 E2 F3000
# Layer change: retract, short travel, restart -- two reversals within one ramp
G1 E-1 F6000
G1 X30.5 F12000
G1 E1.05 F6000
# Bleed paliers: eight short perimeter segments hand the deduction back
G1 X31.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X32.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X33.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X34.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X35.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X36.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X37.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X38.5 E1.25 F12000
# Next retract lands right after the last palier -- the densest pair
G1 E-1 F6000
G1 X39 F12000
G1 E1.05 F6000
G1 X49 E2 F3000
# Second cycle, like consecutive layers on a small part
G1 E-1 F6000
G1 X49.5 F12000
G1 E1.05 F6000
G1 X50.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X51.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X52.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 X53.5 E1.25 F12000
G1 E-1 F6000
G1 X54 F12000
G1 E1.05 F6000
G1 X64 E2 F3000
# Off with a non-zero offset pending: it must come back down its own ramp.
# M400 first: batch mode defers process_move to lookahead flushes, and without
# a flush here the whole scenario would be planned with coef already 0.
M400
SET_PRESSURE_ADVANCE BACKLASH_COEF=0
G1 X74 E2 F3000
